ugh the sky you can never fade into  a red dwarf or collapse into a black  hole even if sometimes you might want to  today is the fifth Sunday an epiphany  the Christian season of stars it's the  season after christmas in the church  calendar the season when we remember the  star that the wise men followed to jesus  and it's the season we read starry  scriptures like the ones today from  Psalms and Isaiah you will not be  surprised to learn that the authors of  Psalms and Isaiah defines stardom a  little differently than Ingrid Bergman  and Lady Gaga and Yale today I'm going  to talk a little about their version of  stardom but before I do there's  something I have to tell you it's a  little personal but it's important for  you to know according to the Bible you  are a star I am a star we are all stars  when God promised Abraham that God would  give him descendants as numerous as the  stars in the sky he was talking about us  our congregation is a constant  think about it okay let's hear what the  psalmist and the prophet have to say  about being stars listen God determines  the number of the stars God gives to all  of them their names God stretches out  the heavens like a curtain and spreads  them like a tent to live in lift up your  eyes on high and see who created these  God brings out their hosts and numbers  them calling them all by name because  god is great and strength mighty in  power not one is missing so according to  the scriptures what does it mean to be a  star or maybe a better question is what  does it mean to be stars because the  first thing we learned about stars is  that there are a lot of them and they  get talked about together and what makes  them so bright is not their individual  glow but their collective glory it's the  way they come together in constellations  and gather in galaxies the stars are a  mass gospel choir of light and they  don't sing solo the book of Job tells us  that when God laid the cornerstone of  the earth the morning stars sang  together and all the heavenly beings  shouted for joy if you're a star shining  and God sky you are not like Hedy Lamarr  shining cold and alone and settling for  just three friends instead you are part  of a heavenly host joining your light  and voice to the rest of the universe  part of the brightness and beauty of all  of God's creation throughout time and  space you are basking in the brightness  of the stars around you  and they are basking and the brightness  of you and together you are making  celestial harmonies and forming yourself  into dazzling patterns when you're  working in your dorm room late at night  you might think that you're alone you  might think that the paper you're  writing only matters to you and your  professor or maybe it just only matters  to you you might think that the only  light you're producing is the faint  light shining from your laptop screen  and whatever dim logical illumination  you can shine on macroeconomics or the  history of sexuality but if you are a  star in God's heaven and you're shining  for God's glory the work that you're  doing in your dorm beams a stream of  light that joins with a light of stars  all over the sky it joins the glow  emitted by an immigrant and East Haven  who is battling police brutality with  courage and faith it joins the gleam of  a sleep-deprived mother in India who is  praying for healing for her sick toddler  and it joins the luminescence of unknown  saints across the world and throughout  the ages who'd pride and are trying to  do God's will and together you all make  a pattern you might not even know about  your combined light illuminates this  dark world and helps the lost navigate  in the night it's not a competition it's  a constellation  the other important thing to know about  stars is that they are all named by God  God creates them all and calls them all  by name ladygaga may have needed to  create herself through a monstrous  effort and she may have needed to rename  herself as well but most of us can rest  secure in the knowledge that we already  exist we are already stars and we are  already ourselves because we have been  named and called by God Isaiah tells us  about the vast universe of stars with  God given names to tell us something  important about ourselves and each other  if God has named all the stars if God's  eye is on the sparrow if God clothes the  lilies of the field if not a hair can  fall from our head without God's  knowledge then we are not just  interchangeable balls of energy burning  at a certain temperature and emitting a  certain amount of light instead we are  castor and pollux ass tyrion and talitha  borealis Nashira and sinistra Regulus  and serious we are shell and Bobo  Heather and lauren james and Jonathan  Kaitlin and Kevin Annabelle and Abby  Marilyn and Debbie Michelle and Jamie we  are all shining together and we are each  known and loved and called by name from  the beginning of the world maybe you  remember the moment when you were a kid  and you realized that everyone else had  thoughts and feelings too and that they  were just as important as yours it's  still so overwhelming and necessary to  realize that there are as many  perspectives as there are people and  that every name represents a being  created by God if we are all stars than  we need to lift our eyes on high  and see each other as the heavenly  beings that we are we need to see each  other through starry eyes and when we do  we will see every crowd every class  roster every list of contacts every  email list every list of the imprisoned  or deported or wounded or dead as a  picture of a shining night sky each name  is eternal and luminous and precious we  need to keep reminding ourselves that we  are all glorious and luminous that we  are all called to shine out with all of  God's children everywhere because  sometimes this can be hard to see with  the naked eye there is a lot of light  pollution these days and the fluorescent  lights of Yale and the neon of Hollywood  can blind us to some of the stars that  we most need to see the star in the East  that guides us to Jesus the north star  that guides us out of slavery into  freedom and the cluster of stars shining  next to us on the Pew I'm going to leave  you with some inspired words from Earth  Wind and Fire that will hopefully stick  in your head this week and remind you to  remember who you really are if you find  yourself in need why don't you listen to  these words and he'd be a giant or grain  of sand words of wisdom are yes I care  you're a shining star no matter who you  are shining bright to see what you could  truly be or in the words of the Apostle  Paul be blameless and innocent children  of God without blemish in the midst of a  crooked and perverse generation in which  you shine like stars in the world  sisters and brothers let's not ask for  the moon  or the Sun or the spotlight or the  limelight we have God and we have each  other we have the Stars amen
 

